==========================================================================
PART 1 — exact verification of the product edge formula e=e(G)n(H)+n(G)e(H)
==========================================================================
K3 (unit triangle):  n=3, e=3, rho=e/n=1  (avgdeg 2)
W7 (hex rosette):    n=7, e=12, rho=12/7  (avgdeg 24/7)

 K3[]K3            (=u(9) maximizer)
   N=9 (expect 9), U=18 (expect 18),  3N=27,  U < 3N,  REGULAR deg 4

 W7[]K3            (=AMP u(21) extremal K3#W7)
   N=21 (expect 21), U=57 (expect 57),  3N=63,  U < 3N,  deg 5..8

 K3[]K3[]K3 = H(3,3) (the n=27 tie)
   N=27 (expect 27), U=81 (expect 81),  3N=81,  U = 3N,  REGULAR deg 6

 W7[]W7            (product that BEATS 3N)
   N=49 (expect 49), U=168 (expect 168),  3N=147,  U > 3N,  deg 6..12

  => product formula e(G[]H)=e(G)n(H)+n(G)e(H) verified exactly (Q(sqrt3)).
  => K3^[]3 = Hamming H(3,3): 27 pts, 6-REGULAR, U=81=3*27 EXACTLY (the tie).

==========================================================================
PART 2 — product census: smallest N where a product TIES / BEATS 3N
==========================================================================
 criterion: product on N=a*b (best factors=u-maximizers) gives U=u(a)b+a u(b),
            U/N = rho(a)+rho(b);  TIE iff rho(a)+rho(b)=3, BEAT iff >3.

 first TIES (U=3N), N<=60:
   N= 27 = 3x9: U = u(3)*9+3*u(9) = 81 = 3N  [rho 1+2=3]
   N= 30 = 3x10: U = u(3)*10+3*u(10) = 90 = 3N  [rho 1+2=3]
 first BEATS (U>3N), N<=60:
   N= 32 = 2x16: U = 98 > 96 = 3N  [rho 1/2+41/16=49/16]
   N= 33 = 3x11: U = 102 > 99 = 3N  [rho 1+23/11=34/11]
   N= 34 = 2x17: U = 103 > 102 = 3N  [rho 1/2+43/17=103/34]
   N= 35 = 5x7: U = 109 > 105 = 3N  [rho 7/5+12/7=109/35]
   N= 36 = 3x12: U = 117 > 108 = 3N  [rho 1+9/4=13/4]
   N= 38 = 2x19: U = 119 > 114 = 3N  [rho 1/2+50/19=119/38]

  => smallest product TIE  at N = 27  (and 30)
  => smallest product BEAT at N = 32  (G2[]K16)
  => N* in [25,28] < 32  =>  N* is NOT a product (a rigid 2D blob).

